+# HUD Kit export plan
+
+Source: Figma page **HUD Kit** (node `30:1`), exported to `design/figma/hud-kit.json`
+(file version `2208815566419836712`, last modified 2026-11-02). Every visual on the page is listed
+below. Each one is either **Native** (we build it from Roblox UI objects, so the artist exports
+nothing) or **Image** (the artist exports it from Figma and uploads it).
+
+## Ground rules for every image
+
+- **Scale.** The page is a 1920 x 1080 frame, so Figma pixels map 1:1 to our 1080p reference size.
+  `Screen.luau` grows the UI with one `UIScale` up to **2x** on a 4K screen and never shrinks it.
+  Every image is therefore exported at **2x** its Figma size. All sizes in this document are
+  the final PNG sizes at 2x unless marked "@1x".
+- **Format.** PNG with a transparent background. Turn off the page/frame background fill before
+  exporting.
+- **Max side 1024 px.** Roblox shrinks larger uploads. Only the logo goes over this limit, so it is
+  split into two images (see below).
+- **Alpha bleed.** Roblox sets fully transparent pixels to black on upload, which shows up as a
+  dark fringe around soft edges. After exporting from Figma, run every PNG through an alpha-bleed /
+  dilate step (an alpha-bleed tool, or Photoshop "Solidify"). This matters most for the glow, the
+  logo, the dot tile, and all white icons.
+- **One-color art is exported in white** (`#FFFFFF`, fully opaque) and colored in game with
+  `ImageColor3` / `ImageTransparency`. The designer's colors are listed in this plan as tint values.
+  Multicolor art keeps its colors.
+- **Sprite sheets.** Build each sheet in Figma as a frame at @1x on a regular grid, then export the
+  frame at 2x. Each cell has a 4 px transparent margin (2 px @1x) around the art so neighboring
+  pieces don't bleed into each other when scaled. The sprite rect covers the art only, not the
+  margin: `ImageRectOffset = (col * cell + 4, row * cell + 4)`, `ImageRectSize = art size`.
+  Columns and rows start at 0.
+- **Common ImageLabel properties** (apply everywhere unless a row says otherwise):
+  `BackgroundTransparency = 1`, `Image = "rbxassetid://<id>"`, `Size` = the @1x display size in
+  offsets (the `UIScale` does the rest), `ImageColor3 = 255,255,255` for multicolor art.
+- **Upload** under the group/account that owns the experience. Record every asset id, sheet
+  size, cell size and sprite rect in one asset module when code starts. The id columns
+  below are there to fill in as uploads finish.
+- Keep the exported PNGs next to the design data in `design/figma/exports/` (new folder) so a
+  re-export starts from the same files.
+
