+## 9-slice images (one image each)
+
+A 9-slice image is stretched by Roblox. Its corners keep their size, its edges stretch along one axis, and
+its middle stretches both ways. `SliceCenter` is the rectangle (in PNG pixels) that stretches.
+Since the art is exported at 2x, `SliceScale = 0.5` draws the corners at their Figma size at 1080p, and
+the `UIScale` takes them back up to full resolution on 4K.
+
+These have to be **single uploads, not sheet pieces**, because `ScaleType = Slice` works on the
+whole image.
+
+### `PanelOrnate`: dialog background (`40:137`)
+
+Designer note: *"Dialog background. Stretches to fit its content, from 240 x 160 up to 960 x 640.
+Corner flourishes must not stretch."*
+
+- Build a **112 x 112 @1x** export frame. Use the panel's fill (`#211B14`) and its 4 px inside gold stroke
+  (`#D9AC51`), and put the four 48 x 48 corner flourishes (`40:84`–`40:87`) in the four corners,
+  oriented exactly as in the design. That leaves a 16 px plain strip between the corners.
+- Export → **224 x 224** px, multicolor.
+- ImageLabel: `ScaleType = Slice`, `SliceCenter = Rect.new(96, 96, 128, 128)`, `SliceScale = 0.5`,
+  `ImageColor3 = 255,255,255`. Size the label to fit its content, kept between 240 x 160 and 960 x 640.
+  The smallest size is well over the 96 x 96 that the two corners need together, so the corners never overlap.
+
+### `SlotEmpty`: empty inventory slot (`40:139`)
+
+Designer note: *"Empty inventory slot. Slot size is a player setting from 80 to 128."* Roblox
+can't draw dashed strokes (2 px, dashes 8 / gaps 6, radius 12), so this is an image.
+
+- Export the slot frame at its design size **96 x 96 @1x** with the stroke in **opaque white**
+  (the design's 30 % opacity is set in game). Lay out the dashes symmetrically, so each corner
+  arc is the same and each side starts and ends the same way.
+- Export → **192 x 192** px.
+- ImageLabel: `ScaleType = Slice`, `SliceCenter = Rect.new(24, 24, 168, 168)` (the 12 px corners
+  stay fixed), `SliceScale = 0.5`, `ImageColor3 = 255,255,255`, `ImageTransparency = 0.7`,
+  `Size` = the player's slot size (80–128 square).
+- Why 9-slice: the corner radius (12) and stroke width (2) stay exactly as designed at every slot
+  size. The cost is that the dashes stretch along the sides (see Gaps).
+
+### `CardRibbon`: ribbon shape (`40:141`)
+
+The corners have different radii: Figma `[16, 0, 16, 0]` means top-left 16, top-right 0,
+bottom-right 16, bottom-left 0. `UICorner` can only round all four corners the same, so the shape is baked.
+
+- Export a **48 x 48 @1x** rectangle with those corner radii, filled **white**.
+- Export → **96 x 96** px.
+- ImageLabel: `Size = UDim2.fromOffset(240, 56)` (or sized to content), `ScaleType = Slice`,
+  `SliceCenter = Rect.new(32, 32, 64, 64)`, `SliceScale = 0.5`, `ImageColor3 = 222, 67, 82`
+  (design fill `#DE4352`). Exporting it in white means every ribbon color uses the same image.
+- The **"NEW" label is native**: a TextLabel child, Builder Sans ExtraBold 22, white, centered.
