+## Single images
+
+### `BadgeLegendary` (`40:145`)
+
+The badge is a circle with a **diamond gradient** (`#FFD94D` → `#D9590D`) and a white star.
+Roblox's `UIGradient` has no diamond mode, so the badge is baked whole.
+
+- Export the 64 x 64 frame → **128 x 128** px, multicolor.
+- ImageLabel: `Size = UDim2.fromOffset(64, 64)`, `ScaleType = Fit`, `ImageColor3 = 255,255,255`.
+- It's the only rarity badge on the page, so it gets its own image. If more rarities are designed,
+  put them all on one `RarityBadges` sheet with 136 px cells (128 art + 4 px margins).
+
+### `Logo` (`40:148`)
+
+The logo is the wordmark with a 6 px outside stroke plus the block mark, all under an orange drop-shadow glow
+(radius 24, `#FF9A1A` at 80 %). A glow that follows the shape is baked into the image.
+
+- Export bounds must include the stroke and glow, not just the group's 640 x 240 box. Wrap the
+  group in a **704 x 256 @1x** frame placed at x 1208, y 456 on the page (the art plus glow
+  covers about x 1210–1910, y 456–710). Check in the export preview that the glow isn't clipped
+  on any side.
+- At 2x that's 1408 x 512, which is over the 1024 limit. **Split it down the middle** into two
+  frames of 352 x 256 @1x (page x 1208–1560 and 1560–1912):
+  - `LogoLeft` → **704 x 512** px
+  - `LogoRight` → **704 x 512** px
+- Draw them as two ImageLabels in a 704 x 256 container: left at `Position = (0, 0)`, right at
+  `Position = UDim2.fromOffset(352, 0)`, each `Size = UDim2.fromOffset(352, 256)`,
+  `ScaleType = Stretch`, `ImageColor3 = 255,255,255`. Positions must be whole pixels so no
+  seam shows.
+- Alpha bleed is required here: the soft orange glow will turn dark at the edge without it.
+
+### `Glow` (`40:159`)
+
+The glow is a 120 x 120 ellipse, `#FFC83C` at 60 %, with a 30 px layer blur. Roblox has no layer blur, so it's baked.
+
+- Build a **180 x 180 @1x** frame (the blur spreads about 30 px past the ellipse on each side)
+  with the ellipse centered, filled **opaque white**. Check that the blur isn't clipped.
+- Export → **360 x 360** px, white, alpha-bled.
+- ImageLabel: `Size = UDim2.fromOffset(180, 180)`, centered on the spot where the ellipse sits
+  (`AnchorPoint = (0.5, 0.5)`), `ScaleType = Stretch`, `ImageColor3 = 255, 200, 60`,
+  `ImageTransparency = 0.4`.
+
+### Item portraits (`40:150`)
+
+Designer note: *"120 item portraits in total, and more are added every update. The item detail
+pane shows one at a time at 128 x 128."* They show one at a time out of a big, growing set, so each
+portrait is **its own image**. A sheet would load 119 portraits nobody is looking at and would need
+re-uploading every update.
+
+- Export each portrait **square, without the rounded corners**. The 12 px rounding is done in game.
+  Size **256 x 256** px (128 @1x x 2).
+- File name `ItemPortrait_<Name>.png` (e.g. `ItemPortrait_Torch.png`). The page shows Torch
+  (`40:120`), Ladder (`40:121`), Door (`40:122`), Fence (`40:123`), Chest (`40:124`) and Bed
+  (`40:125`). All 120 and any future portraits follow the same spec.
+- ImageLabel: `Size = UDim2.fromOffset(128, 128)`, `ScaleType = Crop` (matches Figma's FILL),
+  `ImageColor3 = 255,255,255`, plus a child `UICorner` with `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0, 12)`.
