+## Gaps for the designer to sign off
+
+1. **Slot dashes stretch.** With the 9-slice, the dash and gap lengths along each side scale from
+   about 0.8x (80 px slot) to 1.4x (128 px slot) of the design's 8 / 6. The radius and the 2 px stroke
+   stay exact. If that isn't acceptable, we export one image per allowed slot size instead.
+2. **Glass Card blur** is approximated with an opaque fill (see above). Roblox has no per-frame
+   background blur.
+3. **Logo is two images** to stay sharp at 4K under Roblox's 1024 px limit. The alternative is one
+   1024 x 372 image, which looks slightly soft on 4K.
+4. **Xbox LB/RB/LT/RT** are drawn as circles in the design. Real Xbox bumpers and triggers are
+   pill/trigger shapes, so the designer may want to confirm before export.
+
+## Artist checklist
+
+1. Export each sheet, 9-slice, tile and single image at the sizes above (2x, PNG, transparent).
+2. Alpha-bleed every PNG.
+3. Upload under the experience's owner and send back the asset ids. Fill them into the
+   tables above (or hand them to whoever writes the asset module).
+4. After upload, check in game at 1080p and at 4K (UIScale 2): each image loads, nothing looks blurry
+   at 4K, there's no dark fringe, every sprite rect lands on its piece, the dot tile keeps 24 px spacing,
+   and the panel and slot corners don't stretch.
+5. Check the four sheets on a real phone too. Some phones/consoles have been reported drawing sprite
+   rects on the wrong piece while desktop drew them correctly.
